## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design an edge-friendly, few-shot adaptable vision system with robust localization under real-time constraints and production-domain data shifts.

## Key Concepts

- Edge-efficient architectures, few-shot adapters
- Synthetic+real data for defect distribution
- Temporal consistency and localization losses

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: forward pass outline
function forward(frame, adapter) {
  const feat = backbone(frame);
  const heatmap = detectorHead(feat);
  const adapted = adapter(feat);
  const localized = fuse(heatmap, adapted);
  return localized;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate real-time performance on hardware with varying thermal conditions?
- What failure modes require monitoring in production and how would you mitigate them?

## Why This Is Asked
This assesses end-to-end CV system design on monocular input, 3D reconstruction, semantic/kinematic outputs, and on-device adaptation, under real-world constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular depth/3D reconstruction
- Voxel-based 3D representation and BEV outputs
- Multi-task objectives: occupancy, semantics, motion tracking
- Self-supervision with ego-motion and photometric consistency
- Lightweight 3-shot on-device adaptation via adapters

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation sketch
async function runPipeline(frame) {
  const latent = encode(frame)
  const voxels = decodeToVoxels(latent)
  return { occupancy: voxelToOccupancy(voxels), beings: trackPedestrians(latent) }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you evaluate 3D occupancy accuracy vs. GT? 
- How would you extend to multi-camera fusion or hinge on motion blur?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests few-shot, on-device adaptation, and robust pose estimation under occlusion and motion.

## Key Concepts
- Few-shot on-device adaptation; - monocular 6-DoF pose; - temporal consistency; - synthetic-to-real data.

## Code Example
```javascript
function weightedLoss(posePred, poseGT, maskPred, maskGT){
  const Lp = l2(posePred, poseGT);
  const Lm = crossEntropy(maskPred, maskGT);
  return Lp + Lm;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend to more than 3-shot adaptation with minimal latency?
- How would you evaluate failure modes under strong motion blur and fabric reflectivity?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design end-to-end computer vision systems that fuse perception with physics for deformable objects in cluttered environments, while also demonstrating expertise in efficient on-device adaptation.

## Key Concepts
- On-device few-shot adaptation
- 2.5D depth and surface normals representation
- Differentiable physics for stiffness estimation
- Grasp affordance learning with temporal consistency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: training loop for temporally-consistent affordance learning
for (batch of data) {
  const pred = model.forward(images);
  const affordanceLoss = computeBCE(pred.heatmap, target.heatmap);
  const depthLoss = computeL1(pred.depth, target.depth);
  const physicsLoss = computePhysicsConsistency(pred.stiffness, pred.depth);

  const totalLoss = affordanceLoss + depthLoss + physicsLoss;
  optimizer.step(totalLoss);
}
